User Message: }}}Solve for $x$: $3x+7=16$.\\
\par{\color[rgb]{0.07421875,0.4609375,0.73828125}\definecolor[named]{%
pgfstrokecolor}{rgb}{0.07421875,0.4609375,0.73828125}{{Assistant Message: }}}%
To solve for $x$, we need to isolate x on one side of the equation. We can do %
this by following these steps:
\par\begin{enumerate}\par\enumerate@item@Subtract 7 from both sides of the %
equation: $3x+7-7=16-7$ \\
$3x=9$
\par\enumerate@item@Divide both sides of the equation by $3$: $\dfrac{3x}{3}=%
\dfrac{9}{3}$ \\
$x=3$
\end{enumerate}\par So, the solution is x = 3.
